 <sect1 id="release-18-7">
  <title>Release 18.7</title>

  <formalpara>
  <title>Release date:</title>
  <para>2026-11-12</para>
  </formalpara>

  <para>
   This release contains a variety of fixes from 18.6.
   For information about new features in major release 18, see
   <xref linkend="release-18"/>.
  </para>

  <sect2 id="release-18-7-migration">
   <title>Migration to Version 18.7</title>

   <para>
    A dump/restore is not required for those running 18.X.
   </para>

   <para>
    However, several different bugs have been discovered that could result
    in index corruption.  Examine the changelog entries below that
    mention <command>REINDEX</command>, and reindex any indexes you have
    that might be affected.
   </para>

   <para>
    Also, existing incremental backup files should not be trusted, thanks
    to the discovery of several ways that they could become corrupt.
    It's recommended that users of incremental backups take a new full
    backup after updating and use it as the basis for subsequent
    incremental backups.
   </para>

   <para>
    Also, if you are upgrading from a version earlier than 18.6,
    see <xref linkend="release-18-6"/>.
   </para>
  </sect2>

  <sect2 id="release-18-7-changes">
   <title>Changes</title>

   <itemizedlist>

