Branch: REL_14_STABLE [376324afd] 2026-11-09 06:21:02 -0800
-->
     <para>
      Harden more memory-size calculations against integer overflow
      (Álvaro Herrera)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;317b7bcab">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;f1b226dee">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> Project thanks
      Hillai Ben Sasson, Jayden Sarveshkumar, and Mehmet Ince
      for reporting this problem.
      (CVE-2026-120139)
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Robert Haas <rhaas@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [6f6e4a955] 2026-11-09 06:20:33 -0800
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [c5dc8b0a0] 2026-11-09 06:20:38 -0800
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [4fb349500] 2026-11-09 06:20:43 -0800
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [55c00bffe] 2026-11-09 06:20:48 -0800
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [19cff5432] 2026-11-09 06:20:53 -0800
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [74bb8aa8c] 2026-11-09 06:20:57 -0800
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [9bb8b360f] 2026-11-09 06:21:01 -0800
-->
     <para>
      Fix type confusion in set-returning functions that
      return <type>RECORD</type>, when materialized in a query's target
      list (Melanie Plageman, Robert Haas)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;4fb349500">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The same tuple descriptor was used across multiple calls, which is
      unsafe since the actual record type could vary.
     </para>

     <para>
      The <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> Project thanks
      Peter Geoghegan
      for reporting this problem.
      (CVE-2026-120141)
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [ff2e66f49] 2026-11-09 06:20:32 -0800
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [fd4e840b6] 2026-11-09 06:20:38 -0800
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [6b1ca1333] 2026-11-09 06:20:43 -0800
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [3a3eb7616] 2026-11-09 06:20:48 -0800
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [cac94a040] 2026-11-09 06:20:53 -0800
