     <para>
      Fix use of externally-controlled format string
      in <application>pg_basebackup</application> (Peter Eisentraut)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;af250ef26">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This problem could only be reached if files with unusual names exist
      in the server's data directory.
     </para>

     <para>
      The <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> Project thanks
      Peter Eisentraut
      for reporting this problem.
      (CVE-2026-16240)
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Geoghegan <pg@bowt.ie>
Branch: master [a32b8dc98] 2026-10-06 18:21:39 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [18740523a] 2026-10-06 18:21:37 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [882fd416d] 2026-10-06 18:21:35 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [74f26a193] 2026-10-06 18:21:33 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [80c32ab93] 2026-10-06 18:21:31 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [de0d4f0b1] 2026-10-06 18:21:29 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [469713804] 2026-10-06 18:21:27 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Disable btree index de-duplication support for the
      <type>bpchar</type> data type (Shihao Zhong, Peter Geoghegan)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;882fd416d">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Index de-duplication is unsafe for <type>bpchar</type> because its
      notion of equality is weaker than bitwise equality.  In particular,
      because <type>bpchar</type> equality ignores trailing spaces, values
      of different lengths can compare equal.  De-duplication then allows
      index-only scans to return subtly wrong results.
     </para>

     <para>
      This patch disables de-duplication for new index entries, but does
      nothing about possible corruption of existing entries.  Therefore,
      users who have btree indexes on <type>bpchar</type> columns
      should <command>REINDEX</command> them after installing this update.
     </para>

     <para>
      Note that this problem only applies to columns declared
      as <type>bpchar</type>, that is, lacking any length constraint.  The
      more common usage of <type>CHAR(<replaceable>n</replaceable>)</type>
      is not at risk, even though it shares the same underlying code,
      because the length constraint forces otherwise-equal strings to have
      the same length and thus to be bitwise equal.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Geoghegan <pg@bowt.ie>
Branch: master [8637383f5] 2026-08-19 13:46:45 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [adf440cbe] 2026-08-19 13:46:44 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [b0a36462b] 2026-08-19 13:46:42 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [d778f00c1] 2026-08-19 13:46:40 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [fb7c2a514] 2026-08-19 13:46:38 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [76c05f508] 2026-08-19 13:46:36 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [0bace7af3] 2026-08-19 13:46:34 -0400
Branch: master [a13cdbd3d] 2026-08-19 12:31:09 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [6ee9a8b39] 2026-08-19 12:31:07 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [9900966c7] 2026-08-19 12:31:05 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [af7cbf4e2] 2026-08-19 12:31:03 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [dd1634ddb] 2026-08-19 12:31:01 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [076151080] 2026-08-19 12:30:58 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [fbf889de9] 2026-08-19 12:30:56 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Ensure that <literal>VACUUM</literal> cleans up all dead tuples in a
      GIN index (Peter Geoghegan)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;b0a36462b">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;9900966c7">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      When a single <literal>VACUUM</literal> operation requires multiple
      index scans (because it is removing more tuples than it can hold in
      memory at once), it was possible to miss removing some index entries
      that should be removed.  An additional bug involving a race with
      leaf page splits had the same effect.  These bugs would eventually
      lead to a corrupt index with entries pointing at unrelated table
      rows.
      <command>REINDEX</command> is recommended if you suspect this has
      happened.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Geoghegan <pg@bowt.ie>
Branch: master [f20c42783] 2026-08-22 14:50:40 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [b13fd2899] 2026-08-22 14:50:39 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [9448c3e7b] 2026-08-22 14:50:37 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [aa14281fd] 2026-08-22 14:50:35 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [4dd227f51] 2026-08-22 14:50:33 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [aef6198af] 2026-08-22 14:50:30 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [bbe7aca31] 2026-08-22 14:50:28 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix GIN posting tree page deletion after an incomplete page split
      (Peter Geoghegan)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;9448c3e7b">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The deletion step could incorrectly disconnect sibling pages,
      causing subsequent index searches to miss rows.
      <command>REINDEX</command> is recommended if you suspect this has
      happened.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [27417270a] 2026-10-28 14:21:59 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [c4b2f037d] 2026-10-28 14:22:09 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [e4807a0f3] 2026-10-28 14:22:17 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [b3852eec6] 2026-10-28 14:22:27 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [17c5a0659] 2026-10-28 14:23:17 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [cb51daa27] 2026-10-28 14:23:26 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [9a56e080f] 2026-10-28 14:23:31 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix failure to update mutable <structname>pg_index</structname>
      fields for TOAST-table indexes (Bharath Rupireddy)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;e4807a0f3">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      <command>REINDEX CONCURRENTLY</command> can change these fields, but
      the relation cache was not expecting that, allowing index updates to
      be missed.  The end result could be errors about <quote>missing
      chunk number</quote> due to missing index entries.  Fortunately,
      these only represent index corruption; the TOAST table itself is
      fine, so a <command>REINDEX</command> will suffice to recover.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
