     <para>
      Fix assorted planner bugs triggered by lateral references
     (Richard Guo)
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;cbec57291">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;30baaacdd">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;b7866c934">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;d8a311e8d">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;96c869df7">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;7432ecba1">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;707b3738d">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;01a9e573f">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;d7938ff30">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;77c4a9037">&sect;</ulink>
     <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;17b45abef">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      These mistakes could lead to incorrect query plans causing wrong
      answers, or to internal planner errors such as <quote>failed to
      build any N-way joins</quote>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [0d6103e53] 2026-10-14 12:11:55 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [9d7d4424c] 2026-10-14 12:10:56 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [64fb20a52] 2026-10-14 12:09:56 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [854f81f07] 2026-10-14 12:06:40 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [ca4273866] 2026-10-14 12:07:16 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Ensure proper placement of qual clauses containing PlaceHolderVars
      by assigning a relation ID to antijoins made from SubLinks (Richard
      Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;64fb20a52">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This avoids edge cases where such a qual could be pushed into the
      right-hand side of the antijoin, giving it the opposite of the
      desired semantics.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [c1c930376] 2026-10-30 10:49:26 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [d1e045baf] 2026-10-30 10:50:44 +0900
