Branch: master [35d3f2069] 2026-09-08 10:04:37 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [729e4a322] 2026-09-08 10:06:06 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [e0f5f79d2] 2026-09-08 10:07:14 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [f2e9e3aa1] 2026-09-08 10:09:08 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [071fb9af2] 2026-09-08 10:10:54 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [a9875e35e] 2026-09-08 10:12:33 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [627081c73] 2026-09-08 10:13:50 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix placement of PlaceHolderVars as nestloop parameters
      (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;e84fb3f1c">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;e0f5f79d2">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      In rare cases, planning could fail with <quote>failed to assign all
      NestLoopParams to plan nodes</quote>, <quote>plan should not
      reference subplan's variable</quote>, or <quote>variable not found
      in subplan target list</quote> errors.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [456ee1804] 2026-10-21 15:37:31 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [f366c2ce1] 2026-10-21 15:38:35 +0900
