     <para>
      Avoid planner failure for sort keys that are PlaceHolderVars
      (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5fb5bef3e">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;f6642a97f">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Depending on the plan shape selected, such cases could produce
      wrong results, or could fail with <quote>variable not found in
      subplan target lists</quote>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [f40028994] 2026-10-29 11:27:12 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [4567d170f] 2026-10-29 11:28:08 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [27a53c857] 2026-10-29 11:28:39 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [ba7127f24] 2026-10-29 11:29:08 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [78bc3b96c] 2026-10-29 11:29:34 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix incorrect dropping of outer join clauses after re-associating
      outer joins (Richard Guo, Nitin Motiani)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;27a53c857">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [372761e05] 2026-10-07 14:35:01 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [618130028] 2026-10-07 14:36:24 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [53b058d3b] 2026-10-07 14:37:42 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [0c4235013] 2026-10-07 14:38:42 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [f73794bc1] 2026-10-07 14:39:41 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid <quote>unsupported join alias expression</quote> failures when
      a whole-row Var references a join and appears below an outer join
      (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;53b058d3b">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [bfa1a69ed] 2026-10-04 12:06:24 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [3ad05dea1] 2026-10-04 12:07:30 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [7a776fc9d] 2026-10-04 12:08:11 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [6c0698339] 2026-10-04 12:08:45 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [6bd71489d] 2026-10-04 12:09:20 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [5a7312587] 2026-10-04 12:09:57 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [10717fe15] 2026-10-04 12:10:33 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Handle SubLinks correctly when expanding a whole-row join alias
      reference (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;7a776fc9d">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This oversight led to errors like <quote>cannot handle unplanned
      sub-select</quote> or <quote>unrecognized node type</quote>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [89e06d782] 2026-10-14 16:38:15 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [cbcccca71] 2026-10-14 16:38:15 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [ebf82fae6] 2026-10-14 16:38:15 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Do not perform self-join elimination with inheritance trees
      (Tender Wang)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;ebf82fae6">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      In traditional table inheritance, a unique index on the parent
      table isn't sufficient to prove uniqueness across its children too,
      so that the proof required for SJE isn't possible.  Moreover, the
      code was willing to merge <literal>parent_table</literal>
      with <literal>parent_table ONLY</literal>, which doesn't even
      represent the same set of rows.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [8f2b598b4] 2026-10-15 12:42:45 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [86ce68d9e] 2026-10-15 12:42:45 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [10b2d9986] 2026-10-15 12:42:46 -0400
-->
     <para>
      In self-join elimination, check that clauses used to prove
      uniqueness actually match (Tender Wang)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;10b2d9986">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Previously, this code assumed that equality clauses with the same
      operands were equivalent; but in fact they could use different
      equality operators, or more likely different collations.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [1bf74c806] 2026-08-25 10:16:58 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [d446ca2c4] 2026-08-25 10:18:18 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [4c66f172a] 2026-08-25 10:19:22 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [a4eb938b3] 2026-08-25 10:20:00 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [8fc5b57ae] 2026-08-25 10:20:38 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [201f7192e] 2026-08-25 10:22:12 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [7e29fcd1a] 2026-08-25 10:23:02 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Don't assume that <literal>DISTINCT ON</literal> ensures uniqueness
      of a subquery's output rows when the subquery's targetlist contains
      any set-returning functions (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;4c66f172a">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This doesn't follow, because the set-returning functions may be
      evaluated after the de-duplication step.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [e17df18a8] 2026-09-14 17:03:41 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [acd8d3e0f] 2026-09-14 17:05:29 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [29aef0f68] 2026-09-14 17:07:17 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [23088673d] 2026-09-14 17:08:17 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [27ef9097b] 2026-09-14 17:09:12 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix incorrect constant-folding of a <literal>JSON</literal>
      constructor with a <literal>RETURNING</literal> clause inside a
      simple-form <literal>CASE</literal> with a constant test expression
      (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;29aef0f68">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [264ddc9a6] 2026-09-02 15:32:54 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [a3bc7f2c0] 2026-09-02 15:33:37 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [dd7c135bb] 2026-09-02 15:34:18 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix test for pushing <literal>WHERE</literal> clauses down past a
      grouping step that has a different equivalence rule (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;dd7c135bb">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The previous release cycle's fix for this situation misbehaved for
      some clauses involving <literal>CASE</literal> expressions.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [32872d0c9] 2026-09-18 11:02:10 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [0d5505a22] 2026-09-18 11:02:10 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [720d3df25] 2026-09-18 11:02:10 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [70d0ac3c9] 2026-09-18 11:02:10 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [a91d664d5] 2026-09-18 11:02:10 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [47c43ffda] 2026-09-18 11:02:10 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [d98b99b2a] 2026-09-18 11:02:10 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix incorrect behavior
      of <literal>MIN()</literal>/<literal>MAX()</literal> index scans
      when query specifies <literal>FETCH ... WITH TIES</literal>
      (Chaitanya Choudhary)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;720d3df25">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The <literal>WITH TIES</literal> option was accidentally copied into
      the sub-SELECT generated to perform the index scan, possibly
      triggering <quote>more than one row returned by a subquery used as
      an expression</quote> errors.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Alexander Korotkov <akorotkov@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [d237a7a83] 2026-09-16 13:09:15 +0300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [0d5621890] 2026-09-16 13:10:03 +0300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [1ac292cb1] 2026-09-16 12:31:02 +0300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [a10d14afc] 2026-09-16 12:44:20 +0300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [a9c9c4f76] 2026-09-16 12:44:32 +0300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [db0208bfc] 2026-09-16 12:45:13 +0300
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [b8e0b45ab] 2026-09-16 12:45:21 +0300
-->
     <para>
      Use the correct collation when unique-ifying a semijoin's righthand
      side (Andrey Rachitskiy)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;1ac292cb1">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This is an issue only if the join's comparison clause uses a
      non-deterministic collation, since all deterministic collations
      agree on string equality.  But if it does, it was possible to
      produce incorrect results with too many rows.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [de5659440] 2026-08-28 15:03:54 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [15ccc2041] 2026-08-28 15:04:49 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [718f28167] 2026-08-28 15:05:35 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix handling of disabled plan node types below single-child Append
      nodes (Tender Wang)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;718f28167">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The Append node failed to copy its child's disabled_nodes count,
      allowing it to possibly be chosen over other alternatives that
      contain no disabled nodes.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Dean Rasheed <dean.a.rasheed@gmail.com>
Branch: master [fb60892f4] 2026-09-15 11:47:05 +0100
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [e7006ecae] 2026-09-15 11:47:06 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [6567f3f1f] 2026-09-15 11:47:07 +0100
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [5b4ebfbfa] 2026-09-15 11:47:08 +0100
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [80c9a58b4] 2026-09-15 11:47:09 +0100
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [cbd2406d0] 2026-09-15 11:47:10 +0100
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [5b6b83cb7] 2026-09-15 11:47:11 +0100
Branch: master [76e9e44b0] 2026-11-04 19:45:39 +0000
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2980e5e4d] 2026-11-04 19:45:39 +0000
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [558c00f96] 2026-11-04 19:45:41 +0000
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [0d83f9e0e] 2026-11-04 19:45:42 +0000
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [b76127a88] 2026-11-04 19:45:43 +0000
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [2c4871093] 2026-11-04 19:45:44 +0000
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [83efe9602] 2026-11-04 19:45:45 +0000
-->
     <para>
      Acquire a predicate lock on conflicting rows during <literal>INSERT
      ... ON CONFLICT</literal> (Zsolt Parragi, Andrey Borodin)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;6567f3f1f">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;558c00f96">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Failure to do this resulted in incorrect behavior in serializable
      mode, allowing concurrent updates that should have failed with a
      serialization error.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Eisentraut <peter@eisentraut.org>
Branch: master [bad882987] 2026-09-14 16:55:14 +0200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [05c4b10fc] 2026-09-14 16:55:09 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [937a0e68c] 2026-09-14 16:47:51 +0200
-->
     <para>
      Fix integer overflow during parallel GIN index build (Ewan Young)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;937a0e68c">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Index keys were stored in an interim data structure whose size field
      was only 16 bits, so that keys larger than 65535 bytes were
      truncated, resulting in crashes or corrupted index entries.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [6e5d5680b] 2026-08-28 13:10:21 +1200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [7a74e5ed9] 2026-08-28 13:10:56 +1200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [7c503d683] 2026-08-28 13:11:23 +1200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [2d8494e24] 2026-08-28 13:11:46 +1200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [a0396c8e3] 2026-08-28 13:12:12 +1200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [1a501b6e2] 2026-08-28 13:12:40 +1200
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [978caef19] 2026-08-28 13:13:04 +1200
-->
     <para>
      Fix incorrect multi-column <literal>RANGE</literal> partition
      pruning (David Rowley)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;7c503d683">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      When performing partition pruning with a <literal>RANGE</literal>
      partitioned table where pruning quals are only present for a leading
      prefix of the partition key, it was possible for partition pruning
      to prune away some partitions that shouldn't be pruned (leading to
      missing some rows that should be found) and/or include some
      partitions that were not needed.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [b9d9e9bcc] 2026-09-18 17:14:21 +1200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [73b0b18f1] 2026-09-18 17:14:59 +1200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [63d9e26c2] 2026-09-18 17:15:30 +1200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [d21d4f1ca] 2026-09-18 17:15:52 +1200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [1d8a93336] 2026-09-18 17:16:22 +1200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [9b8c0f238] 2026-09-18 17:16:47 +1200
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [3d734a059] 2026-09-18 17:17:13 +1200
-->
     <para>
      Fix incorrect pruning of <literal>DEFAULT</literal> partitions in
      range-partitioned tables that use <literal>MINVALUE</literal>
      or <literal>MAXVALUE</literal> bounds (Ewan Young)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;63d9e26c2">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      In some cases the code would incorrectly conclude that
      the <literal>DEFAULT</literal> partition needn't be scanned, causing
      failure to find some rows that should match the query.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [1b5dd3a24] 2026-10-09 11:03:07 +1300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2359968b4] 2026-10-09 11:03:53 +1300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [c7328770b] 2026-10-09 11:04:22 +1300
Branch: master [73e69062c] 2026-10-15 15:49:06 +1300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [9b505ef6c] 2026-10-15 15:49:43 +1300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [57193b3a0] 2026-10-15 15:50:11 +1300
-->
     <para>
      Fix mishandling of run-time partition pruning during EPQ rechecks
      (David Rowley, Zsolt Parragi)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;c7328770b">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;57193b3a0">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This error could result in silently skipping rows that should be
      updated, as well as possible use-after-free accesses.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [eacee6b61] 2026-10-14 14:54:45 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [3f807d6e9] 2026-10-14 14:55:25 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [70ffc30e1] 2026-10-14 14:56:08 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Don't use SubPlan-containing expressions in plan-startup-time
      partition pruning (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;70ffc30e1">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This avoids <quote>SubPlan found with no parent plan</quote> errors
      in edge cases.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [b715192e5] 2026-11-05 10:21:17 +1300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [1c2ba4df3] 2026-11-05 10:21:17 +1300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [bfbb3d842] 2026-11-05 10:21:17 +1300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [9171fca99] 2026-11-05 10:21:17 +1300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [0500fb3ab] 2026-11-05 10:21:17 +1300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [6e8605116] 2026-11-05 10:21:17 +1300
Branch: master [edbe7ffdc] 2026-11-06 20:18:18 +1300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [1c087e616] 2026-11-06 20:18:18 +1300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [744ca40cb] 2026-11-06 20:18:18 +1300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [2a3ac1554] 2026-11-06 20:18:18 +1300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [1d57f6ef7] 2026-11-06 20:18:18 +1300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [21a53865f] 2026-11-06 20:18:18 +1300
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [f72e4686e] 2026-11-06 20:18:18 +1300
-->
     <para>
      Fix problems with queries applying multiple sort keys to a single
      column (David Rowley, Ayush Tiwari)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;bfbb3d842">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;744ca40cb">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Some queries could crash the backend, while in other cases the
      additional sort specifications were ignored.  Ordinarily such
      additional sort specifications are redundant anyway, since the first
      one would fully determine the result ordering.  However, this is not
      necessarily so with non-deterministic collations, or with queries
      using different <literal>ORDER BY</literal> operators.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [303c9b362] 2026-11-02 14:36:38 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [24796e334] 2026-11-02 14:37:22 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5b730e81f] 2026-11-02 14:38:32 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [fcb44c5e5] 2026-11-02 14:39:11 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [06e46b651] 2026-11-02 14:40:19 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [f5b8f05ee] 2026-11-02 14:40:58 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [40a5aa4a7] 2026-11-02 14:41:27 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [9d0081c01] 2026-11-02 15:40:50 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [25b55788d] 2026-11-02 15:41:23 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [1e9c734c2] 2026-11-02 15:41:59 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [064281150] 2026-11-02 15:42:37 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [56fb8ee6e] 2026-11-02 15:43:17 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid possible re-use of stale hash tables when a hashed SubPlan is
      referenced in multiple places (Rahul Yadav)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5b730e81f">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;9d0081c01">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [352734540] 2026-11-04 13:43:17 +1300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [0e58f6d73] 2026-11-04 13:43:17 +1300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [9dd027535] 2026-11-04 13:43:17 +1300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [f79bf8d8f] 2026-11-04 13:43:17 +1300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [083d60e34] 2026-11-04 13:43:17 +1300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [2da9b7f9b] 2026-11-04 13:43:17 +1300
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [e22cec1bd] 2026-11-04 13:43:17 +1300
-->
     <para>
      Ensure that Memoize plan nodes use the correct input collation
      (Shihao Zhong)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;9dd027535">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This matters only when using non-deterministic collations.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Richard Guo <rguo@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [708eb5158] 2026-11-02 10:28:38 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [f39f3f971] 2026-11-02 10:29:54 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [dbe6cf558] 2026-11-02 10:30:52 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [d6f60a031] 2026-11-02 10:31:29 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [b5ad785be] 2026-11-02 10:32:00 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [a7a2cab57] 2026-11-02 10:32:52 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [de7d7d4df] 2026-11-02 10:33:24 +0900
Branch: master [45ff0b4a3] 2026-11-03 09:45:51 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [0fd0e501a] 2026-11-03 09:46:54 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [2bcf2fa49] 2026-11-03 09:48:38 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [db7e885d0] 2026-11-03 09:49:37 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [f1d27a922] 2026-11-03 09:50:13 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [025dac1c9] 2026-11-03 09:51:10 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [63e261b0b] 2026-11-03 09:51:48 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix wrong results from Memoize plans when a Param is a subexpression
      of a cache key (Richard Guo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;dbe6cf558">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;2bcf2fa49">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [8b9ffcb11] 2026-10-14 22:06:30 +1300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [a345db783] 2026-10-14 22:07:25 +1300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [0aba37abf] 2026-10-14 22:07:53 +1300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [04609efb3] 2026-10-14 22:08:21 +1300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [0896fb027] 2026-10-14 22:08:46 +1300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [bd811277c] 2026-10-14 22:09:10 +1300
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [3d6e24626] 2026-10-14 22:09:32 +1300
-->
     <para>
      Fix loss of parallel worker statistics for Memoize plan nodes
      underneath a Gather (Tatsuya Kawata)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;0aba37abf">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Only the statistics since the last rescan of the Gather were
      reported by <command>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</command>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Heikki Linnakangas <heikki.linnakangas@iki.fi>
Branch: master [2866d8c7d] 2026-08-27 14:31:44 +0300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [ba12a202c] 2026-08-27 14:31:58 +0300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [b90eeb29e] 2026-08-27 14:32:07 +0300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [b62206043] 2026-08-27 14:32:09 +0300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [e5e841cc5] 2026-08-27 14:32:11 +0300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [b76b966c2] 2026-08-27 14:32:13 +0300
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [ba2ea49b3] 2026-08-27 14:35:12 +0300
-->
     <para>
      Don't create a shell type if a function definition specifies an
      unknown return type name with array or type modifier syntax (Heikki
      Linnakangas)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;b90eeb29e">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Such cases are surely errors, since you should create the type
      before doing anything advanced with it.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Geoghegan <pg@bowt.ie>
Branch: master [79b101486] 2026-08-26 15:38:17 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [ef89c839c] 2026-08-26 15:38:15 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [74c9832ca] 2026-08-26 15:38:13 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [2ae67ada7] 2026-08-26 15:38:11 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [d03ff3b75] 2026-08-26 15:38:09 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [ea3227bf2] 2026-08-26 15:38:07 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [9a1fa1f36] 2026-08-26 15:38:04 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix snapshot export and import to work properly on a snapshot taken
      during recovery (Peter Geoghegan, Bertrand Drouvot)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;74c9832ca">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The data layout is different in such a snapshot, but the
      export/import logic didn't know that, so that the imported snapshot
      behaved incorrectly.  This led not only to wrong answers within the
      importing transaction, but possibly to persistent data corruption
      due to it setting hint bits incorrectly.
     </para>

     <para>
      This bug is known to be triggered by
      parallel <application>pg_dump</application>, when run on a
      standby server.  In that context it could corrupt both the dump
      output and the standby server's data.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Geoghegan <pg@bowt.ie>
Branch: master [0ebeec35f] 2026-08-20 19:47:32 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [ca99016f9] 2026-08-20 19:47:31 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [3977cde27] 2026-08-20 19:47:29 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [24bf23fe6] 2026-08-20 19:47:27 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [7a392b0f6] 2026-08-20 19:47:25 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [4afe4b564] 2026-08-20 19:47:23 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [e94ba903b] 2026-08-20 19:47:21 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix atomicity problem in transaction snapshot import (Chee Wooson)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;3977cde27">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      There was a window in which onlookers might not see the source
      transaction as still running, possibly allowing wrong decisions
      by <command>VACUUM</command> for example.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [142fd8ff1] 2026-09-26 09:28:12 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [aa60617b6] 2026-09-26 09:28:15 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [753057e34] 2026-09-26 09:28:18 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix import of statistics for columns that are domains over range
      types, multirange types, or <type>tsvector</type> (Michael Paquier)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;753057e34">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The restore logic failed to look through the domain while checking
      applicability of statistics types that are for these data types.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Langote <amitlan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [35b349a53] 2026-10-29 10:38:48 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [1ecc3cee7] 2026-10-29 10:38:40 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [6cb715e2d] 2026-10-29 10:38:34 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [8793978e3] 2026-10-29 10:38:24 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix double parse transformation of <literal>PASSING</literal>
      arguments in <literal>JSON_TABLE</literal> (Ayush Tiwari, Amit Langote)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;6cb715e2d">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This mistake caused unexpected failures such as <quote>unexpected
      non-SELECT command in SubLink</quote>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Langote <amitlan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [e405a46c4] 2026-11-06 16:20:27 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [3d72e63b8] 2026-11-06 16:20:14 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [c7656ac9e] 2026-11-06 17:30:24 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [03550d3cf] 2026-11-06 17:29:36 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix failure to assign collations to <literal>PASSING</literal>
      expressions in <literal>JSON_TABLE</literal> (Venu Kummari)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;c7656ac9e">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This oversight could result in wrong answers or <quote>could not
      determine which collation to use for string comparison</quote>
      errors.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [ab713cdcd] 2026-09-19 20:13:51 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [fdb88a51c] 2026-09-19 20:13:56 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [b8736db6e] 2026-09-19 20:14:00 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [8bccf0159] 2026-09-19 20:14:03 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix usage of toasted text values in the <literal>PASSING</literal>
      arguments of <literal>JSON_TABLE</literal> and related functions
      (Chaitanya Choudhary, Shihao Zhong)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;b8736db6e">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The code failed to apply detoasting, resulting in incorrect output.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Langote <amitlan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [627c4df3b] 2026-11-05 15:27:20 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2f2c923c3] 2026-11-05 15:26:41 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [7150d0fd4] 2026-11-05 15:26:26 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [31af62f38] 2026-11-05 12:42:28 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix NULL result persistence in <literal>JSON_VALUE()
      RETURNING</literal> <type>json</type>/<type>jsonb</type>
      (Srinath Reddy Sadipiralla)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;7150d0fd4">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Once <literal>JSON_VALUE(... RETURNING ...)</literal> with
      a <type>json</type> or <type>jsonb</type> result value returned
      NULL, every later evaluation of the same expression in the same
      statement also returned NULL, whether it should or not.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Langote <amitlan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [ee7cfb99a] 2026-11-05 08:54:19 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [8e5c3d3db] 2026-11-05 08:55:05 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [52033b887] 2026-11-05 08:55:23 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [775e03191] 2026-11-05 08:55:39 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix <literal>ON EMPTY/ERROR</literal> result persistence
      in <literal>JSON_VALUE</literal> and related constructs
      (Jian He, Andrey Rachitskiy)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;52033b887">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      A NULL input could result in returning the value of the previous
      row's <literal>ON EMPTY / ON ERROR</literal> expression.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Langote <amitlan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [17b4e9963] 2026-10-29 09:24:21 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [6839997e3] 2026-10-29 09:24:07 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5209a736a] 2026-10-29 09:23:53 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [6dfe31d48] 2026-10-29 09:23:00 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix handling of failures in <literal>DEFAULT</literal> expressions
      in <literal>SQL/JSON</literal> operations (Jian He)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5209a736a">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      An error arising while executing a <literal>DEFAULT</literal>
      expression could be ignored, instead producing a NULL result.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Langote <amitlan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [b6e41c16f] 2026-10-29 09:59:35 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [67f375edb] 2026-10-29 09:59:22 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [b9a415360] 2026-10-29 09:59:08 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [46798ab1a] 2026-10-29 09:58:54 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix handling of domain coercion failures
      in <literal>SQL/JSON</literal> operations (Jian He)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;b9a415360">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      <literal>SQL/JSON</literal> query functions could throw an error, or
      report the wrong one, in cases where an <literal>ON ERROR</literal>
      or <literal>ON EMPTY</literal> clause specified some non-error
      behavior.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [1b0b45c5a] 2026-10-24 14:27:12 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [d44852026] 2026-10-24 14:27:12 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [65f3b7096] 2026-10-24 14:27:12 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [19656b77d] 2026-10-24 14:27:12 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [0cf2c7e38] 2026-10-24 14:27:12 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [3b2a60481] 2026-10-24 14:27:12 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [327c5f0e6] 2026-10-24 14:27:12 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix GIN index searches for plain scalar strings in
      strict <type>jsonpath</type> queries (Rui Zhao)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;65f3b7096">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      A <literal>jsonb_ops</literal> index scan for
      a <type>jsonpath</type> such as <literal>strict $ ==
      "scalar"</literal> failed to find table entries that were
      simply <literal>"scalar"</literal>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [b28a2b2bf] 2026-10-13 16:33:35 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [5146b3f75] 2026-10-13 16:33:35 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [154e2f101] 2026-10-13 16:33:35 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [65f1b71c3] 2026-10-13 16:33:35 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [c138ab8a9] 2026-10-13 16:33:35 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [04a8915fa] 2026-10-13 16:33:35 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [d987ad61d] 2026-10-13 16:33:35 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix errors in extraction of GIN index scan conditions from jsonpath
      queries (Tom Lane)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;154e2f101">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      An <literal>AND</literal> operator underneath
      a <literal>NOT</literal> operator could be misimplemented.
      Also a method applied to a literal constant, for
      example <literal>"42".double()</literal>, was not handled correctly.
      These mistakes did not cause visible errors, but the GIN index
      search would miss some or all of the rows that should match.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: John Naylor <john.naylor@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [328a9a173] 2026-10-30 12:31:39 +0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [b0d482b33] 2026-10-30 12:31:39 +0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [03ba8e591] 2026-10-30 12:31:39 +0700
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [9ad421a9b] 2026-10-30 12:31:39 +0700
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [9cba87fe9] 2026-10-30 12:31:39 +0700
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [0496d85f9] 2026-10-30 12:31:39 +0700
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [9e3077ff4] 2026-10-30 12:31:39 +0700
-->
     <para>
      Fix edge-case error in SP-GiST quad-tree <literal>&lt;@</literal>
      searches (John Naylor)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;03ba8e591">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Due to roundoff error, the search might sometimes not descend into a
      quadrant that it needs to search, leading to incomplete query
      results.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: John Naylor <john.naylor@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [eab68b1be] 2026-10-14 18:19:39 +0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [845725890] 2026-10-14 18:19:39 +0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [fc834ccab] 2026-10-14 18:19:39 +0700
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [3d8c50317] 2026-10-14 18:19:39 +0700
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [235e15ec7] 2026-10-14 18:19:39 +0700
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [37ecbb438] 2026-10-14 18:19:39 +0700
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [0e9544439] 2026-10-14 18:19:39 +0700
-->
     <para>
      Fix edge-case failures in SP-GiST quad-tree indexes (Ayush Tiwari)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;fc834ccab">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Roundoff errors could allow searches and insertions to fail
      with <quote>getQuadrant: impossible case</quote> errors.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [3c5a4a867] 2026-10-22 13:51:27 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [0d0d2a13e] 2026-10-22 13:51:27 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [6c4172b34] 2026-10-22 13:51:27 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [e05b7e2a4] 2026-10-22 13:51:27 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [774c47de1] 2026-10-22 13:51:27 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [187051f85] 2026-10-22 13:51:27 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [264c441c4] 2026-10-22 13:51:27 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Accept empty <type>tsquery</type> values in binary input
      (Ayush Tiwari)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;6c4172b34">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      An empty <type>tsquery</type> value is allowed elsewhere,
      but <function>tsqueryrecv()</function> failed.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [e6cac7fab] 2026-08-17 18:09:07 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [1c732c851] 2026-08-17 18:09:07 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [69915dac4] 2026-08-17 18:09:07 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [91989795d] 2026-08-17 18:09:07 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [cdffe3375] 2026-08-17 18:09:07 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [df8b91463] 2026-08-17 18:09:07 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [05556bdf9] 2026-08-17 18:09:07 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Disallow zero-length lexemes and out-of-range phrase distance values
      in binary input of <type>tsquery</type> values (Tom Lane)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;69915dac4">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      These cases were already rejected during text input,
      but <function>tsqueryrecv()</function> omitted making equivalent
      checks.  That allowed accepting values that would fail subsequent
      dump/reload.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [fe5a01097] 2026-10-05 15:45:40 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [cb600aae3] 2026-10-05 15:45:40 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [90cc09f57] 2026-10-05 15:45:40 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [ffbe37115] 2026-10-05 15:45:40 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [d4fae2993] 2026-10-05 15:45:40 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Treat operators-nested-too-deeply errors as soft errors
      in <type>tsquery</type> input and <type>ltxtquery</type> input
      (Tom Lane)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;90cc09f57">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [957d4eae5] 2026-08-13 11:20:27 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [5185e64ae] 2026-08-13 11:20:27 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [a68beda42] 2026-08-13 11:20:27 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [b42d0c310] 2026-08-13 11:20:27 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [1fc1b82b2] 2026-08-13 11:20:27 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [ef9063a88] 2026-08-13 11:20:27 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [39cad0de4] 2026-08-13 11:20:27 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Consistently enforce maximum lengths in <type>tsvector</type>
      and <type>tsquery</type> (Tom Lane)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;a68beda42">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Some places thought the maximum lexeme length
      was <literal>MAXSTRLEN</literal> (2047), while others thought it
      was <literal>MAXSTRLEN-1</literal>.  Fortunately, the looser bound
      is correct, so make them all use <literal>MAXSTRLEN</literal>.
      Likewise, some places were stricter than others about the total data
      length limit, <literal>MAXSTRPOS</literal>.  These fixes avoid
      situations where a validly-constructed value would fail dump/reload.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Daniel Gustafsson <dgustafsson@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [a63df2664] 2026-09-01 10:13:30 +0200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2291b6ffb] 2026-09-01 10:13:30 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [bfb08d094] 2026-09-01 10:13:30 +0200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [3103bdafd] 2026-09-01 10:15:35 +0200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [48af47dcd] 2026-09-01 10:13:30 +0200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [729bac9eb] 2026-09-01 10:13:30 +0200
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [858fb27b6] 2026-09-01 10:13:30 +0200
-->
     <para>
      Fix <function>right()</function> with a length argument
      of <literal>INT_MIN</literal> (-2147483648) (Ewan Young)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;bfb08d094">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Due to integer overflow, the function returned the whole string
      when it should return an empty string.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Nathan Bossart <nathan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [e7ef2cf25] 2026-10-05 14:52:18 -0500
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [a7539c76b] 2026-10-05 14:52:18 -0500
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [dc60d6aa1] 2026-10-05 14:52:18 -0500
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [c0df269c5] 2026-10-05 14:52:18 -0500
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [af42a7a82] 2026-10-05 14:52:18 -0500
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [8851e44ed] 2026-10-05 14:52:18 -0500
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [36e021cb1] 2026-10-05 14:52:18 -0500
-->
     <para>
      Fix <function>pg_blocking_pids()</function> to account correctly for
      relation extension locks (Bertrand Drouvot)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;dc60d6aa1">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [66042bd3e] 2026-10-22 14:39:03 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2dc899f78] 2026-10-22 14:39:06 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [58998c33d] 2026-10-22 14:39:09 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [8af1a12c9] 2026-10-22 14:39:11 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [6f126b328] 2026-10-22 14:39:13 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [e4ac00514] 2026-10-22 14:39:15 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [5259332a6] 2026-10-22 14:39:17 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix 32-vs-64-bit confusion
      in <function>pg_indexam_progress_phasename()</function> (Markos
      Fountoulakis)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;58998c33d">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This function accidentally worked on common hardware, but could
      misbehave on 32-bit or big-endian platforms.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [3b120b1e9] 2026-09-01 11:42:13 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [9efc2f9d8] 2026-09-01 11:42:50 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [ec434db1f] 2026-09-01 11:42:56 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [04c25af21] 2026-09-01 11:43:01 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [55af98a45] 2026-09-01 11:43:08 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [772251744] 2026-09-01 11:43:13 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [f1c6f7ec9] 2026-09-01 11:43:22 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Detect integer overflow in <function>to_char()</function>
      with <literal>V</literal> format (Andrey Rachitskiy)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;ec434db1f">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      If the data value is an integer, and multiplying it by the power of
      ten implied by the <literal>V</literal> format causes integer
      overflow, <function>to_char()</function> silently emitted incorrect
      digits.  Throw an integer overflow error instead.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tomas Vondra <tomas.vondra@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [252432c4c] 2026-11-02 21:49:31 +0100
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [9a1d7f3a6] 2026-11-02 21:51:03 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [1be7010d1] 2026-11-02 21:51:08 +0100
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [c83ddfcfe] 2026-11-02 21:51:12 +0100
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [7e0d03a91] 2026-11-02 21:51:16 +0100
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [6a770f537] 2026-11-02 21:51:21 +0100
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [c48577385] 2026-11-02 21:51:26 +0100
-->
     <para>
      Avoid integer overflow while calculating BRIN minmax_multi distances
      for <type>tid</type> values (Tomas Vondra)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;1be7010d1">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Very large <type>tid</type> values could result in negative
      distances, which would end in making the index inefficient, though
      not actually corrupt.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tomas Vondra <tomas.vondra@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [c230e14b4] 2026-11-02 21:42:53 +0100
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [78721a206] 2026-11-02 20:11:54 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5c8629bb5] 2026-11-02 20:43:20 +0100
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [9ab2a624e] 2026-11-02 20:48:02 +0100
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [444b85032] 2026-11-02 20:52:23 +0100
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [b8d5b9a01] 2026-11-02 20:56:46 +0100
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [174b605f0] 2026-11-02 21:20:09 +0100
-->
     <para>
      Avoid overflow while calculating BRIN minmax_multi distances
      for numeric values, and handle NaNs properly (Kirill Reshke,
      Tomas Vondra)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5c8629bb5">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      These oversights could result in errors being thrown (preventing
      index summarization), or in inefficient indexes.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tomas Vondra <tomas.vondra@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [d06ac896f] 2026-11-05 15:20:20 +0100
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [1137ebf22] 2026-11-05 15:20:43 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [8a043da94] 2026-11-05 15:21:03 +0100
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [dfd98ce58] 2026-11-05 15:21:22 +0100
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [5c78685fc] 2026-11-05 15:21:42 +0100
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [10686da4e] 2026-11-05 15:22:03 +0100
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [52f418f1f] 2026-11-05 15:22:25 +0100
-->
     <para>
      Avoid overflow when computing differences for numeric ranges
      (Kirill Reshke)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;8a043da94">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      In this context we want to return plus or minus infinity rather than
      throwing an overflow error.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [15ee73d7d] 2026-08-29 19:56:49 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [50daffb06] 2026-08-29 19:56:49 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [1f02a1e48] 2026-08-29 19:56:49 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [e96b27296] 2026-08-29 19:56:49 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [5827ddfc2] 2026-08-29 19:56:49 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [1eca8b94d] 2026-08-29 19:56:49 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [b4c8afdfa] 2026-08-29 19:56:49 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Support out-of-order <literal>FLAG</literal> lines in Hunspell affix
      files (Ewan Young)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;1f02a1e48">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Hunspell affix files usually put the <literal>FLAG</literal> line
      first, and our implementation silently depended on that.  If it came
      after some lines whose meaning depends on
      the <literal>FLAG</literal> setting, the result would be crashes or
      failures to match compound words.  Fix the logic so that
      the <literal>FLAG</literal> line can be anywhere.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [1999fe227] 2026-10-20 17:32:31 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [763f95c63] 2026-10-20 17:32:31 -0400
