     <para>
      Fix assorted errors in rule deparsing (Henson Choi)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;e79df9dd9">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;eb1454ecc">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;b08c4df3b">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;17a0604c2">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Always print <literal>AS</literal> before a target-relation alias
      in <literal>UPDATE</literal>, <literal>DELETE</literal>,
      or <literal>MERGE</literal>, to avoid ambiguity if that alias
      is <literal>set</literal>.  Also ensure
      that <literal><replaceable>xml</replaceable> IS DOCUMENT</literal>
      constructs and subquery left-hand arguments are adequately
      parenthesized.
      Also fix deparsing of <literal>AT TIME ZONE</literal> and similar
      constructs in a view's <literal>FROM</literal> clause; these need
      to be wrapped in a no-op <literal>CAST</literal>.
      These errors could prevent dump restoration due to a syntax error in
      a view, or cause reloaded views to be parsed as something different
      from before.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Langote <amitlan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [ba3115d83] 2026-11-05 08:16:50 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [667243c02] 2026-11-05 08:16:40 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [fa0806647] 2026-11-05 08:16:26 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [f11673768] 2026-11-05 08:16:20 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [2dd680013] 2026-11-05 08:16:12 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [861a9c402] 2026-11-05 08:15:37 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [9e77656a9] 2026-11-05 08:11:17 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix parser failure when a multi-row <command>INSERT
      ... VALUES</command> has a sub-SELECT in a target column subscript
      (Amit Langote)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;fa0806647">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This led to <quote>unexpected non-SELECT command in SubLink</quote>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Nathan Bossart <nathan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [a14041d43] 2026-10-06 09:04:32 -0500
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [63e33d40b] 2026-10-06 09:04:32 -0500
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [95d960447] 2026-10-06 09:04:32 -0500
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [6b428e47b] 2026-10-06 09:04:32 -0500
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [1955fd0b4] 2026-10-06 09:04:32 -0500
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [1adbe902a] 2026-10-06 09:04:32 -0500
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [c596e189d] 2026-10-06 09:04:32 -0500
-->
     <para>
      Fix missed preprocessing of <literal>WHERE</literal> clauses
      in <literal>COPY FROM</literal> (Nathan Bossart)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;95d960447">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This oversight led to <quote>cache lookup failed for
      function 0</quote> errors with negated operators, and probably in
      other cases as well.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [700b422af] 2026-10-27 19:46:12 +1300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [a01d1a17e] 2026-10-27 19:46:42 +1300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [35f60e5ce] 2026-10-27 19:47:09 +1300
-->
     <para>
      Disallow <literal>NOT NULL NO INHERIT</literal> constraints on
      partitioned tables (David Rowley, Nitin Motiani)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;35f60e5ce">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This was already rejected by plain <command>CREATE TABLE</command>,
      but cases such as <command>CREATE TABLE LIKE</command> missed
      checking copied constraints, potentially allowing a partition to
      contain null values when it should not.
     </para>

     <para>
      If you suspect this might have happened in your database, issue this
      command to find broken constraints:
<programlisting>
SELECT conrelid::regclass, conname
FROM pg_constraint
WHERE contype = 'n' AND connoinherit
      AND conrelid IN (SELECT oid FROM pg_class WHERE relkind = 'p');
</programlisting>
      Unwanted constraints can be removed with <literal>ALTER TABLE
      ... DROP CONSTRAINT ...</literal>, while ones that are wanted should
      be repaired with <literal>ALTER TABLE ... ALTER CONSTRAINT
      ... INHERIT</literal>.  The latter command will fail if any null
      values are present in the table's partitions.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [dd97e0c8e] 2026-10-06 13:13:47 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [5e3245401] 2026-10-06 13:14:49 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5659e549a] 2026-10-06 13:14:58 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix test for an existing NOT NULL constraint in <command>ALTER
      TABLE ADD PRIMARY KEY</command> (Fujii Masao, Manuel Reyes Bravo)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5659e549a">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Previously, dropping a NOT NULL column, adding a new column with the
      same name, and making it a primary key in a single <command>ALTER
      TABLE</command> command could fail with <quote>primary key column
      ... is not marked NOT NULL</quote>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Dean Rasheed <dean.a.rasheed@gmail.com>
Branch: master [85f55534e] 2026-09-23 09:39:04 +0100
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [fe1d5aeff] 2026-09-23 09:39:05 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [ce9bd103e] 2026-09-23 09:39:06 +0100
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [745152e45] 2026-09-23 09:39:07 +0100
-->
     <para>
      Fix concurrent delete handling in <command>MERGE ... WHEN NOT
      MATCHED BY SOURCE</command> (Tender Wang)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;ce9bd103e">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      When executing a <literal>WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE</literal>
      action in <command>MERGE</command>, if the tuple from the target
      table was concurrently deleted, the retry code would incorrectly
      execute a <literal>WHEN NOT MATCHED BY TARGET</literal> action for
      the row instead, giving incorrect results.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Andrew Dunstan <andrew@dunslane.net>
Branch: master [a12600b76] 2026-09-09 11:03:39 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [5dec175fb] 2026-09-09 11:06:47 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [d77627daa] 2026-09-09 11:08:39 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [960b6b532] 2026-09-09 11:15:22 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [749dd8d1f] 2026-09-09 11:23:25 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [00126dede] 2026-09-09 11:27:58 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [539b7e829] 2026-09-09 11:32:37 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix race conditions with <command>DROP TABLESPACE</command>
      (Ayush Tiwari)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;d77627daa">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      A <command>DROP</command> executed concurrently with commands that
      attempt to add new objects to the tablespace could end with
      inconsistent catalog contents.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Masahiko Sawada <msawada@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [1e707d325] 2026-10-21 10:44:03 -0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2f79b0179] 2026-10-21 10:44:06 -0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [794c29dc4] 2026-10-21 10:44:09 -0700
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [17f66a681] 2026-10-21 10:44:12 -0700
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [044887b60] 2026-10-21 10:44:14 -0700
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [c517dbb31] 2026-10-21 10:44:17 -0700
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [599c50d25] 2026-10-21 10:44:20 -0700
Branch: master [fded90eec] 2026-10-21 11:10:35 -0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [702f218cb] 2026-10-21 11:10:38 -0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [a5b925cfc] 2026-10-21 11:10:41 -0700
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [3e53104dc] 2026-10-21 11:10:44 -0700
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [391fded1e] 2026-10-21 11:10:46 -0700
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [7f641940c] 2026-10-21 11:10:49 -0700
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [e16d102a4] 2026-10-21 11:10:52 -0700
-->
     <para>
      Cleanly reject operations on unlogged tables during recovery
      (Jim Jones)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;794c29dc4">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;a5b925cfc">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      An unlogged table will have no data on a standby, so reading it must
      fail.  Most operations give an appropriate error for this,
      but <command>COPY ... TO</command> failed with an
      internal <quote>could not open file</quote> error, as
      did <function>currtid2()</function>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Nathan Bossart <nathan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [a8261c766] 2026-08-13 16:35:07 -0500
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [9db2383e0] 2026-08-13 16:35:07 -0500
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [0468246f5] 2026-08-13 16:35:07 -0500
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [be0076b71] 2026-08-13 16:35:07 -0500
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [dbda203fe] 2026-08-13 16:35:07 -0500
-->
     <para>
      Fix inconsistent permissions checking for role membership changes
      (ChangAo Chen)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;0468246f5">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This fixes cases where what should be a permissions failure was
      reported as an internal <quote>no possible grantors</quote> error.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Alexander Korotkov <akorotkov@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [3bed1f91a] 2026-09-08 14:09:20 +0300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [d0518cb3e] 2026-09-08 13:32:52 +0300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5d63dbd97] 2026-09-08 13:32:53 +0300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [bee33974e] 2026-09-08 13:32:54 +0300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [a8004e161] 2026-09-08 13:32:55 +0300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [89834e3f2] 2026-09-08 13:32:56 +0300
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [35e4b760a] 2026-09-08 13:32:57 +0300
-->
     <para>
      Revert previous changes to free space map persistence (Alexander
      Korotkov)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5d63dbd97">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Commits c06d1a4ba et al. (included in the May 2026 releases) turned
      out to cause more trouble than they fixed.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [0b776de09] 2026-09-03 12:12:42 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [e65f21a27] 2026-09-03 12:14:44 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [d2943b94b] 2026-09-03 12:15:17 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [4639b6cfe] 2026-09-03 12:15:23 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [a90cbbc86] 2026-09-03 12:16:05 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [cc1edfa6c] 2026-09-03 12:16:54 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [57c107238] 2026-09-03 12:17:13 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid backend hang during temporary table cleanup at exit, if the
      default transaction mode is <literal>SERIALIZABLE READ ONLY
      DEFERRABLE</literal> (Andrey Rachitskiy)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;d2943b94b">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Cleanup would block until concurrent serializable transactions
      complete, which could be indefinitely if some of them are prepared
      transactions.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [50d6e533e] 2026-10-02 10:43:17 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [7166a1d02] 2026-10-02 10:43:27 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [95f6bfb51] 2026-10-02 10:43:28 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [2affc1964] 2026-10-02 10:43:30 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [caa19f80d] 2026-10-02 10:43:31 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [fc56f1663] 2026-10-02 10:43:33 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [84b86b210] 2026-10-02 10:43:34 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid crash when describing a <command>FETCH</command> statement
      whose cursor is gone (Dirkjan Bussink)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;95f6bfb51">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [85adc584e] 2026-10-06 01:20:57 +1300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [a2148471b] 2026-10-06 01:21:26 +1300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [8d5b228ae] 2026-10-06 01:21:53 +1300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [2414028ab] 2026-10-06 01:22:23 +1300
-->
     <para>
      Fix memory accounting for datum sorts on pass-by-reference data
      types (Mario Karuza)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;8d5b228ae">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This error could lead to failure to
      enforce <varname>work_mem</varname> limits correctly, or to
      misleading output from <command>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</command>.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Heikki Linnakangas <heikki.linnakangas@iki.fi>
Branch: master [96c99955b] 2026-10-05 13:12:33 +0300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [e7d7e047b] 2026-10-05 13:12:42 +0300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5f671c431] 2026-10-05 13:12:44 +0300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [71d1ace33] 2026-10-05 13:12:45 +0300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [226e86cda] 2026-10-05 13:12:46 +0300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [d40546032] 2026-10-05 13:12:47 +0300
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [4a7778ef8] 2026-10-05 13:12:48 +0300
-->
     <para>
      If a vacuum delay sleep is requested while holding locks,
      don't sleep (Kevin Rocker, Andrey Borodin, Mostafa)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5f671c431">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Also, move several existing delay calls to points where it's
      actually safe to sleep.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Masahiko Sawada <msawada@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [abf5fec63] 2026-10-08 11:26:09 -0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2604c28bf] 2026-10-08 11:26:12 -0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [6bfb33088] 2026-10-08 11:26:15 -0700
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [35c508af5] 2026-10-08 11:26:17 -0700
-->
     <para>
      Fix parallel vacuum I/O timing reports (Bharath Rupireddy)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;6bfb33088">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      <literal>VACUUM VERBOSE</literal> and autovacuum logs included
      parallel workers' blocks-read and blocks-dirtied counts, but not the
      time they spent doing that I/O.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Langote <amitlan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [e5f6a7a28] 2026-11-04 15:04:12 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [fbe7033af] 2026-11-04 15:03:58 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [9e9d24c33] 2026-11-04 15:03:44 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [f3ea7cb46] 2026-11-04 15:03:29 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [e37a8075f] 2026-11-04 15:03:15 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [3cb89e214] 2026-11-04 15:02:40 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [bc2125742] 2026-11-04 15:02:04 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid freeing the plan for a foreign-key enforcement query if the
      plan is still in use (Lucas Jeffrey, Trakshan Mishra, Amit Langote)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;9e9d24c33">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      It was possible to reach this behavior in contrived cases, such as a
      self-referencing ON DELETE CASCADE foreign key on tables with
      triggers that perform DML.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [ead8f696b] 2026-08-20 15:17:26 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [386198434] 2026-08-20 15:17:29 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [6a1759a02] 2026-08-20 15:17:32 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix postmaster failing to exit when the startup subprocess crashes
      during crash restart (Zexin Li)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;6a1759a02">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The postmaster should give up and quit in this case, but it failed
      to do so, instead becoming stuck.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [803583ce7] 2026-08-17 08:53:22 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [13967fe0e] 2026-08-17 08:53:24 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [0391fee2d] 2026-08-17 08:53:29 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Be more wary about scanner failures when parsing a GUC file
      (Michael Paquier)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;0391fee2d">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Daniel Gustafsson <dgustafsson@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [e352ac8c5] 2026-11-05 14:14:01 +0100
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [c38de3ae6] 2026-11-05 14:14:01 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [8e54a4145] 2026-11-05 14:14:01 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [dcf112bd4] 2026-11-06 00:49:07 +0100
-->
     <para>
      Recheck <varname>oauth_validator_libraries</varname> during OAuth
      authentication (Zsolt Parragi)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;8e54a4145">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;dcf112bd4">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This addition ensures that changes
      to <varname>oauth_validator_libraries</varname> are enforced
      immediately.  Previously, if such a change made an
      existing <literal>oauth</literal> line
      in <filename>pg_hba.conf</filename> invalid, the new setting was not
      enforced until that situation was fixed.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Daniel Gustafsson <dgustafsson@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [bca67e5a3] 2026-09-17 14:52:30 +0200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [1d094904b] 2026-09-17 14:52:30 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [99c3f5e20] 2026-09-17 14:52:30 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [459ef520d] 2026-09-17 14:56:28 +0200
Author: Jacob Champion <jchampion@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [f1eafd911] 2026-10-08 10:58:07 -0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [08f24a115] 2026-10-08 10:58:14 -0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [af28fc13e] 2026-10-08 10:58:18 -0700
Author: Daniel Gustafsson <dgustafsson@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [8cb6b83e1] 2026-11-05 21:43:55 +0100
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [9f7d6167f] 2026-11-05 21:43:55 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [e83298599] 2026-11-05 21:43:55 +0100
-->
     <para>
      Fix postmaster crash
      when <varname>oauth_validator_libraries</varname> is set to a string
      containing only whitespace (Grigorev Jurij, Zsolt Parragi)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;99c3f5e20">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;459ef520d">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;af28fc13e">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;e83298599">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Geoghegan <pg@bowt.ie>
Branch: master [d42c5457e] 2026-10-26 09:50:58 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [8d5e89328] 2026-10-26 09:50:58 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [e88259b67] 2026-10-26 09:50:58 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [eea2ff293] 2026-10-26 09:50:58 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [4bd8a9613] 2026-10-26 09:50:58 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [eed7bffad] 2026-10-26 09:50:58 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [3651d7c58] 2026-10-26 09:50:58 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix WAL-logging of multi-level page deletion in btree indexes
      (Peter Geoghegan)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;e88259b67">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      The WAL log could contain stale values for a to-be-deleted page's
      sibling links, resulting in complaints on standby servers
      if <varname>wal_consistency_checking</varname> is enabled.  Barring
      a crash, the damage would shortly be repaired by completion of the
      deletion action, so that this error was usually only cosmetic.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [27caf4ca5] 2026-10-29 11:13:44 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [4232bf96e] 2026-10-29 11:13:59 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [7ac2f74d1] 2026-10-29 11:14:10 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [fd1f61e43] 2026-10-29 11:14:34 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid overly-strong WAL consistency check on buffers that are only
      pinned not locked (Greg Burd, Thomas Munro)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;7ac2f74d1">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      A buffer that is not locked could be concurrently changed by other
      processes, so that the image captured for consistency checking is
      not self-consistent, leading to <quote>incorrect resource manager
      data checksum in record</quote> failures on standbys.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [a5ccf2080] 2026-10-26 17:14:07 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2c4a3b3b2] 2026-10-26 17:14:20 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [606f3db55] 2026-10-26 17:14:26 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [15f57b683] 2026-10-26 17:14:35 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [11c87ab37] 2026-10-26 17:14:42 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [4b9009105] 2026-10-26 17:14:53 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [b15c55163] 2026-10-26 17:14:57 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Ensure that state files for pending prepared transactions are
      written out atomically during a checkpoint (Shihao Zhong)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;606f3db55">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Previously it was possible for a crash to leave an invalid state
      file behind, causing subsequent database startup to fail.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [cea96cdfe] 2026-11-02 15:17:57 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [ee189838f] 2026-11-02 15:18:01 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [3a2fc7662] 2026-11-02 15:18:04 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [56e831ea2] 2026-11-02 15:18:09 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [bb4eabd6a] 2026-11-02 15:18:13 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [a39ec399e] 2026-11-02 15:18:17 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [ea1b698f2] 2026-11-02 15:18:21 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Do not start a checkpoint in the middle of aborting a prepared
      transaction (Shihao Zhong)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;3a2fc7662">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      A crash would allow the transaction to be committed afterwards,
      leading to inconsistent state.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Heikki Linnakangas <heikki.linnakangas@iki.fi>
Branch: master [4f3121202] 2026-11-03 01:39:20 +0200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [0035e91dd] 2026-11-03 01:41:34 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [31538e165] 2026-11-03 01:42:07 +0200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [4022edb93] 2026-11-03 01:43:09 +0200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [0d0bde0b0] 2026-11-03 01:43:25 +0200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [8681aef6f] 2026-11-03 01:43:41 +0200
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [67fa8cb33] 2026-11-03 01:53:23 +0200
-->
     <para>
      Do not start a checkpoint in the middle of creating a multixact
      (Shihao Zhong)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;31538e165">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This avoids possible data loss after a subsequent crash.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [e7f4463e8] 2026-10-26 09:54:08 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [928c2eeed] 2026-10-26 09:54:17 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5df84b355] 2026-10-26 09:54:30 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [08f0cec8f] 2026-10-26 09:54:44 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [07d1b4418] 2026-10-26 09:54:50 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [0b5656749] 2026-10-26 09:54:56 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [278d2a672] 2026-10-26 09:55:01 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix possible loss of tuples updated by later-aborted subtransactions
      (Shihao Zhong, Michael Paquier)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5df84b355">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      A table rewrite (for example, <command>CLUSTER</command>
      or <command>VACUUM FULL</command>) could discard such tuples as
      invalid.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Nathan Bossart <nathan@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [8a8ee213d] 2026-11-02 10:13:52 -0600
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [ea11f9464] 2026-11-02 10:13:52 -0600
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [badcb62d6] 2026-11-02 10:13:52 -0600
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [7e594c30f] 2026-11-02 10:13:52 -0600
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [c5c36ae6f] 2026-11-02 10:13:52 -0600
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [a3d1ac495] 2026-11-02 10:13:52 -0600
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [4e9a5dc1f] 2026-11-02 10:13:52 -0600
-->
     <para>
      Do not lose tuple's <type>tid</type> when storing it into a tuple
      table slot (Virender Singla, Greg Burd)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;badcb62d6">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Some code paths neglected to copy the <type>tid</type> field, which
      could lead to data corruption or wrong query answers in unusual
      cases.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Álvaro Herrera <alvherre@kurilemu.de>
Branch: master [2ebd68497] 2026-10-25 10:23:46 +0100
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [57a2e2cf5] 2026-10-25 10:23:46 +0100
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [1735ad557] 2026-10-25 10:23:46 +0100
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [bd8070126] 2026-10-25 10:23:46 +0100
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [3bd5a4755] 2026-10-25 10:23:46 +0100
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [9ab37b6e7] 2026-10-25 10:23:46 +0100
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [31fa77982] 2026-10-25 10:23:46 +0100
-->
     <para>
      Avoid race condition in marking a partitioned index valid (Andrey
      Borodin, Kirill Reshke)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;1735ad557">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This could, for example, cause
      parallel <application>pg_restore</application> to fail due to trying
      to recreate foreign key constraints too soon.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Heikki Linnakangas <heikki.linnakangas@iki.fi>
Branch: master [068c9aaec] 2026-10-15 11:23:06 +0300
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [ad56a7f09] 2026-10-15 11:23:09 +0300
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [94d53e9ec] 2026-10-15 11:23:12 +0300
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [ff9eacc56] 2026-10-15 11:23:13 +0300
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [7cafc4abb] 2026-10-15 11:23:15 +0300
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [f51a03db3] 2026-10-15 11:23:17 +0300
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [623cdfa64] 2026-10-15 11:23:19 +0300
-->
     <para>
      Fix checks for an aborted updating transaction in multixids
      (Chee Wooson)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;94d53e9ec">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Known consequences of this coding error include
      unexpected <quote>new multixact has more than one updating
      member</quote> errors, as well as incorrect failures to update a
      row.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Geoghegan <pg@bowt.ie>
Branch: master [173cf85a0] 2026-10-10 10:26:18 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [c4117066b] 2026-10-10 10:26:18 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [a85b5523e] 2026-10-10 10:26:18 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [ab2233743] 2026-10-10 10:26:18 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [99ae176e4] 2026-10-10 10:26:18 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [1495e2cba] 2026-10-10 10:26:18 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [22be34ac1] 2026-10-10 10:26:18 -0400
-->
     <para>
      A hash index scan that starts during a bucket split could miss some
      index entries (Peter Geoghegan, Amit Kapila)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;a85b5523e">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [374522aa6] 2026-09-24 01:18:37 +1200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [ad230d588] 2026-09-24 01:19:38 +1200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [39a0db101] 2026-09-24 01:20:02 +1200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [25ebf0097] 2026-09-24 01:20:27 +1200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [6ceac2e12] 2026-09-24 01:20:53 +1200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [cd7d3e129] 2026-09-24 01:21:15 +1200
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [c84dd31bd] 2026-09-24 01:21:45 +1200
-->
     <para>
      Fix incorrect position tracking in TID Range Scans (Ewan Young,
      David Rowley)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;39a0db101">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Sequences involving fetching backwards and then forwards again could
      fail to scan all the way to the end of the range.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Melanie Plageman <melanieplageman@gmail.com>
Branch: master [07c73f450] 2026-09-22 18:19:00 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [1139b7eff] 2026-09-22 18:23:40 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [9733eb9e8] 2026-09-22 18:27:25 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [5897bd1d8] 2026-09-22 18:31:08 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Avoid unnecessary buffer locking when recovery replays freeze-only
      and VM-only WAL records (Melanie Plageman)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;9733eb9e8">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This prevents unnecessary replay delays and cancellations of standby
      queries.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [4a92c8c29] 2026-10-28 08:42:35 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [e2c633b43] 2026-10-28 08:42:41 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [8cddd5fc8] 2026-10-28 08:42:52 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [4aeefb26d] 2026-10-28 08:42:57 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [5dc3cfbb9] 2026-10-28 08:43:00 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [316a87065] 2026-10-28 08:43:04 +0900
Branch: master [c97931c16] 2026-10-29 09:43:12 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [9c299e292] 2026-10-29 09:43:28 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [4f857f399] 2026-10-29 09:43:44 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [59bc83d41] 2026-10-29 09:44:07 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [38ecdfdc1] 2026-10-29 09:44:16 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [4b87b605b] 2026-10-29 09:44:23 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [0cfd56254] 2026-10-28 07:54:31 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [d2c1e18de] 2026-10-28 08:00:23 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid reading a potentially-torn copy of
      the <literal>pg_control</literal> file for base backups (David
      Steele)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;8cddd5fc8">&sect;</ulink>
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;4f857f399">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      A concurrent write to the file could result in including
      inconsistent data in the backup.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [51d7bf5ed] 2026-10-27 13:53:26 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2bfed4d18] 2026-10-27 13:53:42 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [b09b26ac8] 2026-10-27 13:53:46 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [1fbe31b9d] 2026-10-27 13:53:52 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [61aec3f3b] 2026-10-27 13:53:59 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [1fff28b14] 2026-10-27 13:54:02 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Prevent making incorrect copies of non-relation files in base
      backups (David Steele)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;b09b26ac8">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Files that routinely get replaced by atomic renames, such
      as <filename>postgresql.auto.conf</filename>, could be truncated
      or zero-padded in a backup made concurrently with such a
      replacement.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [340f2ac62] 2026-08-19 09:51:49 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [db0f6dd80] 2026-08-19 09:51:52 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [39faf4de2] 2026-08-19 09:51:54 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [7f92983dc] 2026-08-19 09:51:56 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [45c88d621] 2026-08-19 09:51:58 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [f555ada9e] 2026-08-19 09:51:59 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [19d900358] 2026-08-19 09:52:01 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Ensure that base backups report checksum failures affecting single
      pages (Zsolt Parragi)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;39faf4de2">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Due to a logic error, checksum failures were counted
      in <structname>pg_stat_database</structname> only when more than one
      page in the same file was corrupt.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [b5545d3f5] 2026-11-05 18:06:25 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [dde54ecde] 2026-11-05 18:07:05 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [41b4b8e8b] 2026-11-05 18:07:17 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [0733c7219] 2026-11-05 18:07:48 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix stale visibility maps in incremental backups after heap
      truncation (Ke, Fujii Masao, Shihao Zhong)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;41b4b8e8b">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      An incremental backup taken after <command>VACUUM</command>
      truncates a table can restore stale visibility map bits when both
      data checksums and wal_log_hints are disabled, leading to data
      corruption.
     </para>

     <para>
      This fix does not correct existing WAL summaries, therefore
      incremental backups taken after updating can still be affected.
      It's recommended that users of incremental backups take a new full
      backup after updating and use it as the basis for subsequent
      incremental backups.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [316861101] 2026-11-03 13:03:38 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [04ea11d0e] 2026-11-03 13:04:50 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [2afbad0ce] 2026-11-03 13:04:57 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [ecb43083f] 2026-11-03 13:05:04 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Reject incremental backups based on a backup from a divergent
      history (Sai Pranav, Fujii Masao)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;2afbad0ce">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      After a failover, an incremental backup could accept a prior backup
      whose WAL range extends beyond the point where the new primary left
      the old timeline.  Combining these backups could retain pages from
      the abandoned history, producing a corrupt backup.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [d903620ac] 2026-11-02 00:22:09 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2bae29d7e] 2026-11-02 00:23:01 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [9e20db542] 2026-11-02 00:23:07 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [9580e29da] 2026-11-02 00:24:02 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Ensure that incremental backup merges WAL summaries in LSN order
      (Ke, Fujii Masao)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;9e20db542">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This error could result in stale data being included in a combined
      backup.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [f549ecd26] 2026-11-02 00:17:17 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [ed89d84ed] 2026-11-02 00:18:13 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5787f8785] 2026-11-02 00:18:40 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [ec756e591] 2026-11-02 00:19:44 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix erroneous edge-case decisions about when to include WAL
      summaries in incremental backups (Ayush Tiwari)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5787f8785">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This error could result in stale data being included in a combined
      backup.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [cedd2cec7] 2026-10-14 19:55:24 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [97fa9bdc5] 2026-10-14 19:56:13 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [f47c63d7a] 2026-10-14 19:56:40 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [4c674b952] 2026-10-14 19:56:45 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix incorrect size estimates for incremental backups
      (Daria Lepikhova)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;f47c63d7a">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This problem affected progress reporting
      in <application>pg_basebackup</application> and other places.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Kapila <akapila@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [fc1900915] 2026-11-05 09:49:17 +0530
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [1e1a4821a] 2026-11-05 09:42:16 +0530
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [fbaebf450] 2026-11-05 09:38:18 +0530
-->
     <para>
      Avoid resetting a replication
      subscription's <literal>two_phase</literal> state to pending if it
      is already enabled (Zhijie Hou)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;fbaebf450">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Executing <literal>ALTER SUBSCRIPTION ... SET (two_phase =
      true)</literal> twice resulted in confused state, potentially
      allowing data corruption on the subscriber.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Jacob Champion <jchampion@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [161d5ffcc] 2026-11-05 16:52:56 -0800
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [aad726131] 2026-11-05 16:53:34 -0800
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [e2b3549a4] 2026-11-05 16:53:48 -0800
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [7c78c8cff] 2026-11-05 16:54:21 -0800
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [079638030] 2026-11-05 16:54:37 -0800
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [d0571ca16] 2026-11-05 16:54:46 -0800
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [0c8611c6e] 2026-11-05 16:54:52 -0800
-->
     <para>
      Verify the syntax of the <varname>output_plugin_libraries</varname>
      parameter when a value is assigned (Jacob Champion, Hayato Kuroda)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;e2b3549a4">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Previously, a syntactically-incorrect value could be put
      into <filename>postgresql.conf</filename>, causing logical
      replication to fail.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Álvaro Herrera <alvherre@kurilemu.de>
Branch: master [bdaad789c] 2026-08-12 19:15:48 +0200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [82c86ac68] 2026-08-12 19:15:48 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [864ef0fb1] 2026-08-12 19:15:48 +0200
-->
     <para>
      Reject <literal>REPLICA IDENTITY USING INDEX</literal> if a key
      column has an unvalidated <literal>NOT NULL</literal> constraint
      (Ante Kresic)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;864ef0fb1">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      A replica identity key must be not-null, but this code path would
      accept cases where that was not yet known to be true.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Kapila <akapila@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [3cde90ecc] 2026-10-21 08:50:02 +0530
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [48b43081e] 2026-10-21 08:42:06 +0530
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [23fffd382] 2026-10-21 08:34:27 +0530
-->
     <para>
      Fix logical replication with a lossy identity index (Paul
      A. Jungwirth, Zhijie Hou)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;23fffd382">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Typically identity indexes are btrees, which deliver exact results.
      However, GiST indexes on multiranges can be used as identity
      indexes, and they deliver results that require rechecking.  Logical
      replication failed to perform the recheck, so that updates and
      deletes could target the wrong row on the subscriber.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [9510a826e] 2026-09-30 14:35:14 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [453ebae70] 2026-09-30 14:37:14 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [c5666f7e1] 2026-09-30 14:37:17 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [295f75b4b] 2026-09-30 14:37:19 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [02c32116d] 2026-09-30 14:37:21 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [3d15afe7d] 2026-09-30 14:37:23 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [56b306f8b] 2026-09-30 14:37:24 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid incorrect update of backend status flags during replication
      slot invalidation (Vlad Lesin)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;c5666f7e1">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      An invalidation done by an auxiliary process such as the
      checkpointer could clobber the status field of an unrelated backend.
      The consequences of this are difficult to predict, but one
      possibility is that hot standby feedback could be effectively
      disabled.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Álvaro Herrera <alvherre@kurilemu.de>
Branch: master [beff3cd00] 2026-10-14 19:42:04 +0200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [963ff022f] 2026-10-14 19:42:04 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5eae2800a] 2026-10-14 19:42:04 +0200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [624bd2b1f] 2026-10-14 19:42:04 +0200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [ff5ba5f19] 2026-10-14 19:42:04 +0200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [0a6dc4fe1] 2026-10-14 19:42:04 +0200
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [83be64488] 2026-10-14 19:42:04 +0200
-->
     <para>
      In logical replication, handle subtransaction aborts better
      (Bingshuai Li, Hayato Kuroda, Zhijie Hou)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5eae2800a">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      If a subtransaction that made a catalog update aborts, logical
      decoding mistakenly still believed that the update was effective,
      potentially causing incorrect decoding output.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Álvaro Herrera <alvherre@kurilemu.de>
Branch: master [46024c573] 2026-09-24 11:52:47 +0200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [4a4bf490d] 2026-09-24 12:24:56 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [6210f00ca] 2026-09-24 11:52:47 +0200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [b93df6eac] 2026-09-24 11:52:47 +0200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [a33ffaf7b] 2026-09-24 11:52:47 +0200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [5ff6a3d3f] 2026-09-24 11:52:47 +0200
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [070e21268] 2026-09-24 11:52:47 +0200
-->
     <para>
      Avoid race condition when building an initial decoding snapshot
      (Antonin Houska, Rui Zhao)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;6210f00ca">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      There was a small risk of data corruption from using a snapshot that
      includes transactions that have committed but not yet set their CLOG
      status.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Masahiko Sawada <msawada@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [aa4c52b80] 2026-08-18 11:56:49 -0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [e4f16fda6] 2026-08-18 11:56:52 -0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [caa463e3f] 2026-08-18 11:56:55 -0700
-->
     <para>
      In logical decoding, avoid processing a stream abort event for a
      subtransaction that was never actually streamed (Andrey Rachitskiy)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;caa463e3f">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This error could lead to null pointer dereferences or other
      misbehavior.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [180f3dcd4] 2026-11-02 08:12:27 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [4fbae9145] 2026-11-02 08:12:34 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [6437d9774] 2026-11-02 08:12:38 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [c3ef3f228] 2026-11-02 08:12:43 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [e8191e13f] 2026-11-02 08:12:47 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [c6cb792e8] 2026-11-02 08:12:50 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [35848657c] 2026-11-02 08:12:53 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid null-pointer crash with missing replication option values
      in <literal>pgoutput</literal> logical replication sender (Zhijie
      Hou)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;6437d9774">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Masahiko Sawada <msawada@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [bb1e3e475] 2026-09-18 10:18:52 -0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [e995b2cb4] 2026-09-18 10:18:55 -0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [a477847eb] 2026-09-18 10:18:58 -0700
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [3d6a4a582] 2026-09-18 10:19:01 -0700
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [feb975917] 2026-09-18 10:19:04 -0700
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [274da088e] 2026-09-18 10:19:07 -0700
-->
     <para>
      Fix small memory leak in <application>pgoutput</application> with
      streamed prepared transactions (Ayush Tiwari)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;a477847eb">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [782d9cf8b] 2026-11-03 10:46:41 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [a9b32f4c8] 2026-11-03 10:47:27 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [1ff9f9380] 2026-11-03 10:47:34 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [6d34d5500] 2026-11-03 10:47:40 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [2ac618d71] 2026-11-03 10:48:12 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix lost wakeups in physical WAL senders (Alex Speller)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;1ff9f9380">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This fix corrects some cases where a WAL sender process could sleep
      even though there is data waiting to be sent.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [58ff54aee] 2026-08-28 01:15:23 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [764d31b8a] 2026-08-28 01:15:59 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [2bf6144b4] 2026-08-28 01:16:04 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [4c8fa02c5] 2026-08-28 01:16:08 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [58fb12f4a] 2026-08-28 01:16:45 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [874c22c94] 2026-08-28 01:17:02 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [aec25d610] 2026-08-28 01:17:19 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix duplicate creation of temporary replication slot when a WAL
      receiver follows a timeline switch (ChangAo Chen)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;2bf6144b4">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This mistake led to a <quote>could not create replication
      slot</quote> error followed by a restart of the WAL receiver, which
      would then recover, so there was no permanent damage.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Kapila <akapila@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [ad36e3608] 2026-09-28 07:17:39 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [2f7bf51b7] 2026-09-28 07:11:29 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [af48a6702] 2026-09-28 06:57:50 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [0405dcf7c] 2026-09-28 06:44:47 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [2389f898e] 2026-09-28 06:52:24 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix race condition between logical replication subscriber and
      concurrent index DDL (Mikhail Nikalayeu, Vignesh C)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;af48a6702">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Changing the state of a replication target relation's primary key or
      replica identity index could cause the replication apply logic to
      miss finding a matching row (but only once per such event).
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [01b3d24c4] 2026-11-03 10:49:40 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [472da35ac] 2026-11-03 10:50:33 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [092da6511] 2026-11-03 10:51:05 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [5f472ab56] 2026-11-03 10:51:47 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [bcb9d9051] 2026-11-03 10:51:55 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [3ec983535] 2026-11-03 10:52:01 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix incorrect LSNs in WAL decoding error messages (Rahul Yadav)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;092da6511">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      These error messages reported the LSN of a WAL record that wasn't
      the one they were actually complaining about.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Amit Kapila <akapila@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [ea9c9432c] 2026-08-27 10:12:53 +0530
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [3c73b272b] 2026-08-27 10:05:51 +0530
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [38eb0cfa3] 2026-08-27 09:54:16 +0530
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [92c018214] 2026-08-27 09:52:28 +0530
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [b3272b49a] 2026-08-27 09:20:41 +0530
-->
     <para>
      Don't allow <literal>REPLICA IDENTITY FULL</literal> lookups to
      select invalid indexes (Mikhail Nikalayeu)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;38eb0cfa3">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Previously, logical replication could try to use an index left
      behind by a failed <command>CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY</command>,
      leading to wrong results since the index is likely incomplete.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [f2dd2a3bd] 2026-10-14 12:05:07 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [d162119ef] 2026-10-14 12:05:11 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [d21a3e1fe] 2026-10-14 12:05:12 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [39173a9bd] 2026-10-14 12:05:14 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [078110c00] 2026-10-14 12:05:15 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [3f82c47b5] 2026-10-14 12:05:17 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [0e2260ab1] 2026-10-14 12:05:18 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix potential use-after-free cases in WAL sender (Ayush Tiwari)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;d21a3e1fe">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: John Naylor <john.naylor@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [e355089a5] 2026-10-19 11:34:06 +0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [cb98b23da] 2026-10-19 11:34:06 +0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [52af12e9d] 2026-10-19 11:34:06 +0700
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [723075b03] 2026-10-19 11:34:06 +0700
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [4a3177299] 2026-10-19 11:34:06 +0700
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [b3477b1ca] 2026-10-19 11:34:06 +0700
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [42b320abe] 2026-10-19 11:34:06 +0700
-->
     <para>
      Avoid use-after-free in <function>jsonb_set_lax()</function>
      (John Naylor)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;52af12e9d">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [01131ca43] 2026-11-01 20:45:51 -0500
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [bfe9c23ee] 2026-11-01 20:45:51 -0500
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [f10500777] 2026-11-01 20:45:51 -0500
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [7fa0a5f21] 2026-11-01 20:45:52 -0500
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [582db3ee0] 2026-11-01 20:45:52 -0500
-->
     <para>
      Fix double-free when <literal>XMLSERIALIZE(... INDENT)</literal>
      output exceeds 1GB (Jim Jones)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;f10500777">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Heikki Linnakangas <heikki.linnakangas@iki.fi>
Branch: master [77705d1e5] 2026-10-31 13:24:50 +0200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [4c0e3c1bf] 2026-10-31 13:24:56 +0200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [d3a03158c] 2026-10-31 13:25:01 +0200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [f1ba2b826] 2026-10-31 13:25:03 +0200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [a2732c986] 2026-10-31 13:25:05 +0200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [bb0615c89] 2026-10-31 13:25:06 +0200
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [275ad2006] 2026-10-31 13:25:08 +0200
-->
     <para>
      Fix null-pointer dereferences that could occur when a schema is
      concurrently dropped (Baji Shaik)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;d3a03158c">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Masahiko Sawada <msawada@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [f3b0bb298] 2026-08-26 12:03:52 -0700
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [4d9224a43] 2026-08-26 12:03:54 -0700
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [ec074c41e] 2026-08-26 12:03:58 -0700
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [ebf7971da] 2026-08-26 12:04:01 -0700
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [ec8aaf845] 2026-08-26 12:04:03 -0700
-->
     <para>
      Avoid null-pointer crash in logical subscription refresh when a
      relevant relation is concurrently dropped (Satyanarayana Narlapuram,
      Bharath Rupireddy)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;ec074c41e">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [4f89416c9] 2026-10-30 17:29:32 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [4b93eec05] 2026-10-30 17:29:35 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [4bcd0d31c] 2026-11-09 06:05:31 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [8b517a30c] 2026-10-30 17:29:43 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [0cea8f85e] 2026-10-30 17:29:50 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [b2ca62b1c] 2026-10-30 17:29:54 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [6ffd2f91b] 2026-10-30 17:29:58 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix possible null-pointer dereference when building extended
      statistics on expressions (Shihao Zhong, Michael Paquier)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;4bcd0d31c">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This error was reachable only with unexpected (but legal) behavior
      of a custom <function>typanalyze</function> function.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [5bd2e236e] 2026-09-28 14:20:27 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [bb356f869] 2026-09-28 14:21:25 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [ccffd3439] 2026-09-28 14:21:31 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [0165f38d1] 2026-09-28 14:22:04 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [6f2f51084] 2026-09-28 14:22:38 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [0ef59b285] 2026-09-28 14:22:43 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [edfa6c8fc] 2026-09-28 14:22:47 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix possibly-stale values of
      <structname>pg_locks</structname>.<structfield>waitstart</structfield>
      (Shihao Zhong)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;ccffd3439">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [16706f1f4] 2026-09-17 19:25:12 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [fc29deb52] 2026-09-17 19:25:21 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [e99e00b27] 2026-09-17 19:25:25 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [6e0011596] 2026-09-17 19:25:27 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [203b96953] 2026-09-17 19:25:30 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [0016a2cc4] 2026-09-17 19:25:32 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Harden pgstats code against partially-completed local pgstats
      entries (Michael Paquier)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;e99e00b27">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [e9d0600ab] 2026-10-21 10:55:21 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [8de334270] 2026-10-21 10:55:29 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [2c056b37f] 2026-10-21 10:55:31 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [1613efa1a] 2026-10-21 10:55:33 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [ae97ef28d] 2026-10-21 10:55:35 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [7a405e5d7] 2026-10-21 10:55:41 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix cleanup of reused pgstats entries (Michael Paquier)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;2c056b37f">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This error led to leakage of pgstats entries, which could result in
      errors at backend exit or database shutdown.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [6a146d297] 2026-11-04 11:16:44 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [a919ea702] 2026-11-04 11:18:01 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [7418d9e96] 2026-11-04 11:18:06 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [aa6f14da4] 2026-11-04 11:18:11 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [4c271dc21] 2026-11-04 11:18:16 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [8b04cc817] 2026-11-04 11:18:20 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix memory leaks caused by not releasing all data associated with a
      WAL reader (Tomás Senart)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;7418d9e96">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      In many cases this oversight did little harm because the containing
      memory context would soon be reset or deleted.  However there are
      cases where it could cause long-lived memory bloat, notably in the
      checkpointer process.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>
Branch: master [6d4607e88] 2026-10-14 10:14:54 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [f51585330] 2026-10-14 10:16:10 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [942266c7f] 2026-10-14 10:16:19 +0900
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [a8c98c884] 2026-10-14 10:16:21 +0900
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [050ad7edb] 2026-10-14 10:16:23 +0900
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [ec6780c59] 2026-10-14 10:16:25 +0900
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [205f40f5b] 2026-10-14 10:16:26 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Avoid memory bloat while computing <literal>ndistinct</literal>
      extended statistics across many columns (Ilia Evdokimov)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;942266c7f">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Peter Geoghegan <pg@bowt.ie>
Branch: master [49103c3cd] 2026-10-14 14:26:04 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [e61e120c1] 2026-10-14 14:26:04 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [f4284d9aa] 2026-10-14 14:26:04 -0400
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [b57161883] 2026-10-14 14:26:04 -0400
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [c180f965d] 2026-10-14 14:26:04 -0400
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [4f45920f0] 2026-10-14 14:26:04 -0400
Branch: REL_14_STABLE [3eaa726e7] 2026-10-14 14:26:04 -0400
-->
     <para>
      Fix buffer pin leak after a failed hash index bucket split cleanup
      (Peter Geoghegan)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;f4284d9aa">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This coding error resulted in nothing worse than warnings about
      resource leakage.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: David Rowley <drowley@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [1051099a9] 2026-08-27 02:40:23 +1200
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [4f0af2635] 2026-08-27 02:41:21 +1200
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [715d83971] 2026-08-27 02:42:01 +1200
Branch: REL_17_STABLE [70d5b0668] 2026-08-27 02:42:32 +1200
Branch: REL_16_STABLE [059aae612] 2026-08-27 02:43:04 +1200
Branch: REL_15_STABLE [c949e6524] 2026-08-27 02:43:34 +1200
-->
     <para>
      Ensure all relations opened for <literal>AFTER</literal> triggers
      are closed again (Hayato Kuroda, David Rowley)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;715d83971">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      This oversight triggered <quote>resource was not closed</quote>
      warnings, but nothing more serious than that.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Fujii Masao <fujii@postgresql.org>
Branch: master [953c6dabd] 2026-11-05 18:02:22 +0900
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [62f868e77] 2026-11-05 18:03:16 +0900
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [5bfe88cf6] 2026-11-05 18:03:44 +0900
-->
     <para>
      Fix <literal>io_uring</literal> resource leakage across crash
      restarts (Lucas Draescher)
      <ulink url="&commit_baseurl;5bfe88cf6">&sect;</ulink>
     </para>

     <para>
      Eventually, a restart would fail with <quote>too many open
      files</quote> or a similar error, at which point the postmaster
      would exit and the resources would be released.  This is only an
      issue when using <literal>io_method=io_uring</literal>, which is not
      the default.
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
<!--
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Branch: master [663c34c1e] 2026-10-26 14:03:23 -0400
Branch: REL_19_STABLE [791446a14] 2026-10-26 14:03:23 -0400
Branch: REL_18_STABLE [a34d61616] 2026-10-26 14:03:24 -0400
